      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "It was established in acute experiments on dogs with the anterior interventricular branch of the left coronary artery ligated in the middle third that isoptin increases essentially the blood flow and oxygen tension in the focus of acute myocardial ischemia, increases the cardiac stroke and minute volumes, and reduces the total peripheral vascular resistance. Strophanthin removes the favourable effect of isoptin on collateral coronary circulation and contractile myocardial activity and increases the total peripheral vascular resistance."},
